    "summary_one_sentence": "When a fading boy-band star steals a heartfelt track from a past-his-prime wedding singer to reignite his solo career, the song's original writer embarks on a desperate quest to reclaim his music and reputation.",
    "summary_short": "Rick is a past-his-prime wedding singer who bonds with fading boy-band star Danny during a late-night jam session. After Rick plays an unreleased, deeply personal track, Danny records it and turns it into a massive comeback hit without giving Rick credit. Facing legal threats from Danny's team, Rick sets out to regain recognition for his work, risking his family stability and friendships in the process. Ultimately, Rick must balance his hunger for artistic validation against the real-life relationships that matter most.",
    "summary_long": "Rick Power is a Dublin-based wedding singer whose early ambitions for musical stardom took a back seat to family life. During a gig, he meets Danny Wilson, a former boy-band idol struggling to establish a solo career. The two bond over drinks and music, during which Rick plays a personal, unreleased song he wrote for his daughter. Months later, Rick is shocked to hear his melody on the radio as Danny's breakout hit, which Danny claims as his own creation. When Danny's label threatens Rick with legal action to silence him, Rick becomes obsessed with reclaiming credit and gets fired from his band after a series of reckless outbursts. Determined to confront Danny, Rick travels to Los Angeles with a friend and crashes Danny's house party to demand recognition. Danny refuses, fundamentally misunderstanding the origin and emotional weight of the track. Returning home empty-handed, Rick reconciles with his family and realizes the true value of making music for his loved ones. Eventually, an old home video surfaces that proves Rick's original authorship, ultimately securing him the recognition and peace of mind he deserved.",
    "synopsis": "Rick Power is a talented singer-songwriter who traded his dreams of rock stardom for a steady life fronting a Dublin wedding band and raising a family. When fading boy-band star Danny Wilson attends one of Rick's gigs, the two strike up a friendship and spend the evening jamming together. During their late-night session, Rick shares a deeply personal song he originally wrote for his young daughter. Months later, Danny records and releases the track as his solo comeback single, taking full credit for the song as it rockets up the charts. When Rick attempts to reach out, Danny's high-powered team shuts him down with legal threats, pushing Rick into a crusade to reclaim his artistic identity. Directed by John Carney, 'Power Ballad' is an uplifting dramedy exploring ambition, authenticity, the music industry, and the enduring strength of family bonds.",
